        <section id="conclusion-start-with-the-date-and-the-guest-count" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-4 border-t border-[#F3E8EA] pt-7">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A] sm:text-3xl">Conclusion: Start With the Date and the Guest Count</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700">An Indian wedding takes a lot of people, and a good Indian Wedding Planning Master Checklist keeps all of them pointed the same way. Pick your date, set your guest count, book the big vendors, and tick off one workstream at a time.</p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700">You don’t need to finish everything today. You just need to know what comes next.</p>
          <p class="rounded-2xl bg-[#1A1A1A] p-5 font-medium leading-relaxed text-white">Next step: open the <a class="font-bold text-[#F4C5CD] underline" href="/tools/wedding-planning-dashboard">Wedding Planning Dashboard</a>, load this Indian wedding planning checklist, and set your first three tasks for this week.</p>
